    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>This magic tapestry can be hung on a wall or another suitable vertical surface. It unravels and reweaves itself to show the content and emotions of your most recent dreams.</p><p>While the tapestry is hung and you are within 30 feet of it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Dream Wisdom.</strong> During a Long Rest, you can spend an hour studying the tapestry. At the end of the Long Rest, roll 1d20 and record the number rolled. Once before you finish a Long Rest, you can replace any D20 Test you make with that number. You must decide to do so before you roll.</p><p><strong>Message Recorder.</strong> If you are targeted by the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDream00000]{Dream} spell, the tapestry weaves the appearance and name of the spell’s caster into its design.</p><p><strong>Mind Wall.</strong> While you have the &amp;Reference[Unconscious apply=false] condition, you have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-wtmx8HtdeXSvuEhG\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Dream Wisdom</em> lance le d20 à noter ; l’Avantage de <em>Mind Wall</em> est à appliquer à la main.</p></section>",
